Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The database schema is defined by the SQLAlchemy models in app/models.py and
versioned by the migration scripts in alembic/versions/. The app no longer
creates tables at startup - Alembic is the single source of truth.

Connection settings come from app/config.py (the .env file). You do not set a
URL in alembic.ini. Override it for a one-off run with the ALEMBIC_DATABASE_URL
environment variable.

Common commands (run from the project root, with the venv active)
----------------------------------------------------------------

  alembic upgrade head              apply all pending migrations
  alembic current                   show the DB's current revision
  alembic history                   list all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1              undo the last migration
  alembic check                     fail if models and DB have drifted

Creating a new migration after changing a model
-----------------------------------------------

  1. Edit app/models.py.
  2. alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
  3. Read the generated file in alembic/versions/ - autogenerate is a draft,
     not a final answer (it misses things like data backfills and some
     server-default changes).
  4. alembic upgrade head

First-time setup on an existing database
----------------------------------------

A database that already had the tables (created before Alembic was added) is
already at revision 0001_baseline. Tell Alembic that once, then upgrade:

  alembic stamp 0001_baseline
  alembic upgrade head

A brand-new empty database just needs:

  alembic upgrade head
